# nano\-vLLM Java models
> borderColor=`#1B2838`,fillColor=`#3D5A80`,mmd.emoticon=`brain`

- FILE
<pre>./models/README.md</pre>
- LINK
<pre>https://github.com/raydac/nano-vllm-java</pre>
- NOTE
<pre>Five graph kinds, one factory. Load with LlmModelFactory.make(path) or open(path).make(), then LLM.builder(model) for a shared matmul pool. Chat uses ChatSession / chatOnce. Non-chat uses typed generate(LlmInput, LlmModality) — TEXT, EMBEDDING, AUDIO, LABELS. Architecture is detected exactly by ModelSupport (no substring matching: qwen3_5 is not qwen3). This map is fully expanded: no topic is collapsed. Follow FILE extras into sources, LINK extras to Hub pages.</pre>

## Chat \(text → text\)
> fillColor=`#7AA3E5`,mmd.emoticon=`comment`,topicLinkUID=`A11CHAT00001`

- FILE
<pre>./nano-vllm-java/src/main/java/com/igormaznitsa/nanollvm/models/internal/CausalLM.java</pre>
- NOTE
<pre>Causal decoder-only graphs: qwen3, gemma3 / gemma3_text, gemma4 / gemma4_text (QAT mobile text), llama / llama2 / llama3, lfm2 (GGUF). Kind.CHAT. Paged KV cache. Usable modality is TEXT→TEXT even when Gemma 4 declares image/audio/video towers.</pre>
```Java
try (LlmModel model = LlmModelFactory.make(Path.of("models/Qwen3-0.6B"));
     LLM llm = LLM.builder(model).deterministic().build()) {
  String answer = llm.chatOnce("Say hello in one sentence.");
}
```

